# kits.txt -- which kit Pis to deploy to
#
# THIS IS A TEMPLATE. Do not edit it in place and do not commit a filled-in
# copy -- it is tracked. Instead, from inside deploy/:
#
#   cp kits.txt.template ./kits.txt
#   chmod 600 ./kits.txt
#   $EDITOR ./kits.txt
#
# REPLACE each <STUB> below with that kit's real IP address, e.g.
#   kit1 <KIT1_IP>     ->     kit1 10.0.0.101
#
# Format:  <kit_name> <ip_address>   -- whitespace separated, one kit per line.
#          Lines starting with # are ignored. Blank lines are ignored.
#
# Add or delete lines so the list matches how many kits you actually have.
# Kit names are free-form but must be UNIQUE -- they label the per-kit
# success/failure output, so duplicates make it impossible to tell kits apart.
#
# deploy_to_kits.sh and copy_file_to_kits.sh both refuse to run while any
# <STUB> remains, so you cannot accidentally deploy against placeholders.

kit1 <KIT1_IP>
kit2 <KIT2_IP>
kit3 <KIT3_IP>
kit4 <KIT4_IP>
kit5 <KIT5_IP>
